<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shankaraji Narayan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1707">1707</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shankaraji Narayan was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deshastha-brahmin">Deshastha Brahmin</a> official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state who was appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv">Sachiv</a>, one of the king's chief ministers, by Rajaram in 1697. He played an important part in the Maratha resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in the hills around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a>. The lands granted to support his office became the princely state of Bhor, held by his descendants as hereditary Pant Sachivs.</p></div>
